# What the local runtime starts: every app's containers, the browser, the
# coding engines and their engine builds (podman --cgroup-parent,
# cseries_runtime/common.py CGROUP_PARENT). The Host, its database, the door
# and the bastion are services in system.slice, beside this one.
#
# CPU: a weight, never a ceiling. When the processors are busy the kernel
# shares them between this slice and system.slice in proportion to their
# weights, 20 here against systemd's default 100 there, so the Host and what
# it needs get at least five sixths of every processor they ask for, and the
# containers, however many and however busy, at least one sixth. When the
# Host leaves processors idle the containers may use all of them: a weight
# takes nothing from anyone until two sides want the same processor. 20 is
# also what podman gives a container's --cpu-shares 512 in cgroup v2, the
# share the runtime meant for its containers against the Host from the start.
#
# A top-level slice on purpose: in "a-b.slice" systemd nests b under a.slice,
# and a weight counts only against siblings.
[Unit]
Description=C-Series runtime containers (apps, browser, coding engines)
Documentation=man:systemd.slice(5) man:systemd.resource-control(5)
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
CPUWeight=20
